cell.lisp rewrites the plugin's runtime half in Common Lisp: the rule family
that names sensitive material (a dotenv or environment read, a credential
directory, an authentication file), an egress-capable command, an upload, a
download run through a shell and a reverse shell; the balanced, strict and
audit modes over that family, with an operator question in balanced mode; the
memory that a sensitive read was let through, which gates a later
egress-capable call; a metadata-only record of the decisions; and a status
and clear command. The plugin scanned a whole tool-call argument object in
Python; this cell prints the form (comments dropped) plus the strings a call
carries and scans that, and it asks through the organism's own question
board.

Left out, because Nodecode has one tool where Hermes had many: the
capability classifier over Hermes's tool names (here the tool is read from
the call's text, with `allow_egress` for a tool that is meant to send), and
`safe_read_roots`, since a call carries no file-read arguments to place
inside a root. Left out, because they are a separate product surface and not
the runtime guard: the behavioral evaluation suite and its OpenAI-compatible
client, `model inspect` against Hugging Face, the model lockfiles, and the
signed fleet admission, key generation and ledger commands. The taint is the
image's, not a session's, since the hook carries no session id.
